# Shaggoth environment variables
# Copy to .env and fill in values, then restart the service.
# The systemd service reads this file automatically (EnvironmentFile=).

# --- Required for GPT replies ---
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...

# --- Optional GPT tuning ---
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_MAX_TOKENS=300

# --- Optional: API key for the HTTP server ---
# When set, all /chat /history /facts routes require:
#   Authorization: Bearer <key>
# SHAGGOTH_API_KEY=your-secret-here

# --- Optional: Cloudflare D1 + KV (cloud backup / push subscriptions) ---
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your-account-id
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your-api-token
# CLOUDFLARE_D1_DATABASE_ID=02e06c82-4187-4116-a0a1-0e5a0ea7b276
# CLOUDFLARE_KV_NAMESPACE_ID=18c863e25c74401594dbc464cb50970d

# --- Optional: Slack notifications ---
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
# SLACK_CHANNEL_ID=C0BLD1P9TC5

# --- Optional: cloud teacher for the self-grading critic loop ---
# The critic (shaggoth/quality/critic.py) grades Shaggoth's own past answers
# on idle capacity and files bad ones for re-research. By default it uses the
# local Ollama on this box (shaggoth/quality/teacher.py::Teacher) -- Shaggoth
# is meant to stay self-hosted, and routing self-improvement through someone
# else's API quietly makes it a wrapper. SHAGGOTH_TEACHER_PROVIDER is an
# explicit, recorded opt-in out of that default; see AGENTS.md for why.
#
# SHAGGOTH_TEACHER_PROVIDER=ollama   # ollama (default) | anthropic | openrouter | auto
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
#
# "auto" cascades: Anthropic -> OpenRouter -> local Ollama, skipping
# whichever cloud provider has no key set. When a provider's judgement call
# fails with a quota/rate-limit/billing error it is skipped for the rest of
# this process's life (restart the service to reset and retry from the top
# -- e.g. after topping up credits). Any other failure (timeout, bad
# response) is retried on that same provider next time, since it isn't
# evidence the provider is actually out.
